# Copy to `.env` beside docker-compose.yml. Docker Compose reads it automatically.

# Which optional services come up with `docker compose up -d`.
#
# Without this you have to remember `--profile mt` on every command, and
# forgetting it on a redeploy silently takes the translator away — the app then
# correctly reports it as unreachable, which reads like a fault rather than a
# missing flag. Set it once instead.
#
# Comma-separated. Available: mt (sentence translation), llm (local Ollama).
# `nlp` and `speech` are declared in the compose file but not implemented yet.
#
# WHAT THESE TWO COST on a first `up`, so the number is not a surprise: `mt`
# builds from source and downloads ~2.4 GB of weights to convert; `llm` pulls
# the Ollama image and then sits idle until YOU pull a model into it
# (`docker exec tanulom-ollama ollama pull qwen3:8b`, ~5 GB). Neither does
# anything until it is switched on in Settings -> Services either — starting a
# container is not the same as enabling the feature. Drop whichever you do not
# want; the core app is complete without both.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=mt,llm
